window.SITE_PAGES = [{"title": "Pinetta Nursery", "url": "./", "text": "Welcome to Pinetta Nursery and our homestead. Our goal is to provide fruit, nuts and support plants for our neighbors in North Florida to enrich their lives by growing some portion of their own food. We are propagating lots of plants in our greenhouse for sale. We are also building a two acre food forest featuring fruit, nuts, herbs and flowering plants. This will be a demonstration area and used as “mother plants” for our propagation efforts. The goal is to have a good blend of perennial crops that can provide a balanced diet. Protein and Fats come from nuts and avocados while carbs from sweet potatoes, peanuts and sunchokes mixed with lots of greens. We have not made the commitment to have any animals as we still like to have the flexibility to travel in our RV."}, {"title": "For Sale", "url": "for-sale/", "text": "Plants Details Picture Fig Trees $15 each / 10 available Mulberry Trees $10 each / 10 available Chocolate Mint $6 / 10 available Gardenia $12 / 25 available Crape Myrtle $10 / 35 available Plants come and go so ask if you are looking for something."}, {"title": "About", "url": "about-us/", "text": "Joe & Rhonda Moraca are living the dream on their third rural property. In between there were several stretches of city life in Sarasota and Gainesville. Before we bought our current property we traveled full time in our RV for about three years. We hit 45 of 50 states in the USA and plan on continuing to travel part-time. We both love rural living and growing plants. Our morning ritual includes a walk around the property picking berries and whatever else we find that is ready to eat. This is some text below the images"}, {"title": "Food Forests", "url": "food-forests/", "text": "yum yum food growing in a forest setting. Interesting video David the Good is a long time Florida Food Forest guy even if he now lives and grows in Alabama."}, {"title": "Contact", "url": "contact-form/", "text": "Please fill in the form below or call Joe Moraca 386-288-9689 This form is not connected yet. The previous site delivered messages through WordPress. This static copy has no database and no mail server, so nothing typed here is saved or sent. Please call Joe Moraca at 386-288-9689 . These fields match the old form so they can be connected to a form service later. Name * First Last Email * Comment or Message Name Message or Submit"}, {"title": "Building a greenhouse", "url": "build-greenhouse/", "text": "We built a 20 x 32 greenhouse. It was a lot of work but well worth the effort. I bought a “kit” that had everything except the doors for each end section. I had to drill “a lot” of holes in that pipe. But the instructions that came with the kit were pretty good. I later bought the shade cloth to block the harsh summer sun and keep it cooler inside."}, {"title": "Irrigation", "url": "irrigation/", "text": "I have installed 9 zones of irrigation with well over 100 emitters. It is a real challenge to design the system to most efficiently but water where it is needed. This we my second “controller” setup. The first one was not as well organized much to my regret. ;-("}, {"title": "How to Start", "url": "how-to-start/", "text": "If you want to have a plant nursery you need plants 😉 I have been purchasing various plant to use as “mother” plants. I take cutting from many of them and start the cuttings."}];
